(a) the period for which personal data will be stored, or criteria for determining that period;
(b) where applicable, the existence of rights to access, rectification, erasure, restriction of processing, and objection;
(c) the right to withdraw consent (where applicable);
(d) the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority;
(e) whether providing the personal data is obligatory or voluntary and the consequences of non-provision;
(g) the existence of automated decision-making, including profiling, and meaningful information about its logic, significance, and consequences.

